---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import FlavorTabs from "../../../components/FlavorTabs.astro";
import ModuleHero from "../../../components/module/ModuleHero.astro";
import ModuleScenario from "../../../components/module/ModuleScenario.astro";
import ModuleFlowDiagram from "../../../components/module/ModuleFlowDiagram.astro";
import HybridSearchDemo from "../../../components/module/demos/HybridSearchDemo.astro";
import ModuleFooterNav from "../../../components/module/ModuleFooterNav.astro";
import ModuleRecap from "../../../components/module/ModuleRecap.astro";
import ModuleQuiz from "../../../components/module/ModuleQuiz.astro";
import { flavor as gcp } from "../../../data/flavors/gcp";
import { flavor as aws } from "../../../data/flavors/aws";
import { flavor as azure } from "../../../data/flavors/azure";
import { flavor as oss } from "../../../data/flavors/oss";
import { MODULES } from "../../../data/modules";

const moduleId = "35-retrieval";
const entries = {
  gcp: gcp[moduleId],
  aws: aws[moduleId],
  azure: azure[moduleId],
  oss: oss[moduleId],
};
const moduleData = MODULES.find((m) => m.id === moduleId)!;
---

<SiteLayout title="35 · Retrieval quality" description={moduleData.summary}>
  <article>
    <ModuleHero moduleId={moduleId}>
      <p>
        A working RAG pipeline finds <em>similar</em> chunks the moment embeddings exist. Retrieval quality is the
        difference between "similar" and "actually relevant" — the gap that separates a demo from something a real
        user trusts.
      </p>
    </ModuleHero>

    <ModuleScenario moduleId={moduleId} />

    <ModuleFlowDiagram moduleId={moduleId} />

    <h2>Hybrid search: BM25 + vector</h2>
    <p>
      Vector search alone misses exact matches — a SKU, an error code, a name — because embeddings encode meaning,
      not tokens. <strong>Hybrid search</strong> runs a keyword method (BM25) alongside vector search and combines
      both rankings. It's the highest-leverage upgrade from Module 15's plain vector index: it fixes the class of
      failures where the right chunk exists but the embedding just wasn't close enough.
    </p>

    <HybridSearchDemo />

    <h2>Rerankers</h2>
    <p>
      Vector and hybrid search are optimized for speed over millions of chunks, which trades away precision. A <strong>reranker</strong> (typically a cross-encoder) re-scores a small candidate set by looking at the query
      and each candidate together, not independently — slower per item, far more accurate:
    </p>
    <div class="concept-flow" role="list" aria-label="Retrieval to reranking pipeline">
      <span class="chip chip--accent" role="listitem">CHEAP RETRIEVAL</span>
      <span class="concept-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <span class="chip" role="listitem">TOP-20 CANDIDATES</span>
      <span class="concept-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <span class="chip" role="listitem">RERANK (cross-encoder)</span>
      <span class="concept-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <span class="chip" role="listitem">PRECISE TOP RESULTS</span>
    </div>

    <h2>Query rewriting and HyDE</h2>
    <p class="concept-comparison-lede">Users don't phrase questions the way documents phrase answers — two ways to close that gap:</p>
    <div class="concept-comparison" role="list">
      <div class="concept-comparison-item" role="listitem">
        <span class="chip chip--accent">QUERY REWRITING</span>
        <p>Expands or reformulates the query before retrieval — synonyms, decomposing multi-part questions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="concept-comparison-item" role="listitem">
        <span class="chip">HyDE</span>
        <p>Ask the LLM to draft a hypothetical answer first, then embed <em>that</em> instead of the raw question — its phrasing tends to resemble real answers more than a question does.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Measuring it: recall and precision</h2>
    <p class="concept-comparison-lede">
      You can't tell if a retrieval change helped without a labeled set — a handful of queries with the correct
      chunk(s) marked ahead of time:
    </p>
    <div class="concept-comparison" role="list">
      <div class="concept-comparison-item" role="listitem">
        <span class="chip chip--accent">RECALL@K</span>
        <p>Is the right chunk in the top k results?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="concept-comparison-item" role="listitem">
        <span class="chip">PRECISION@K</span>
        <p>Of the top k results, how many are actually relevant?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>Module 45 builds this into a full evaluation suite — this module is where you start collecting the labeled examples it will need.</p>

    <h2>Try it in your flavor</h2>
    <FlavorTabs moduleId={moduleId} entries={entries} />

    <h2>Pitfalls</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Shipping vector-only search and assuming it covers keyword-style queries (SKUs, codes, names) — it doesn't.</li>
      <li>Reranking the entire index instead of a small candidate set — cross-encoders don't scale to "rerank everything."</li>
      <li>Tuning retrieval by eyeballing a few queries instead of against a labeled recall/precision set — you'll optimize for the wrong thing.</li>
      <li>Adding HyDE or query rewriting as a default for every query — they add latency and cost, and plain retrieval is often good enough for simple lookups.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
  <ModuleQuiz moduleId={moduleId} />
  <ModuleRecap moduleId={moduleId} />
  <ModuleFooterNav moduleId={moduleId} />
</SiteLayout>
